 "v1_problem": "Dispute ticket volume roughly doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1180-1260/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-03), and the majority of disputed bills are built from ACTUAL meter reads rather than ESTIMATED (1785 vs 1240 of 3025, E-02), while no tariff change occurred (E-04). Current evidence best supports that a change to billing import/validation rules around August altered how both ACTUAL and ESTIMATED reads are accepted during the billing-import step, producing a wave of incorrect bills that drove the dispute surge, with field staffing shortages (E-05, E-07) contributing a secondary, smaller share limited to estimate-substituted accounts.",
